      <Docs>
        <summary>
          <para>The offset represents a position between the children of this position's node, used with AccessibilityNodeInfo.getChild(int). The offset bounds are from 0 to AccessibilityNodeInfo.getChildCount(), inclusive. An offset of 0 represents the position conceptually before the first child, and an offset equal to the child count represents the position after the last child.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/view/accessibility/AccessibilityNodeInfo.SelectionPosition#OFFSET_TYPE_CHILD" title="Reference documentation">Android reference for <code>android.view.accessibility.AccessibilityNodeInfo.SelectionPosition.OFFSET_TYPE_CHILD</code>.</a></format></para>
